207" owner_email="dhsharp@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/07/354207/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibe7d75377e41eb3ae0742adb497e1e048f41067d" commit="79e7edb68adb2b7fafee961de4c0ca761a59dc67" commit_message="pytest: Implement rf_graphyte.  Graphyte is the next-generation RF testing framework. This CL implements the pytest to execute Graphyte.  BUG=b:27819261 TEST=manually  Change-Id: Ibe7d75377e41eb3ae0742adb497e1e048f41067d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/350270 Commit-Ready: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="350270" owner_email="akahuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/70/350270/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ic34d2d578b55e50e8c6004c3241cdafb7789909c" commit="2d988b2c19e080f53dfaca5ebfaa39db0c35e428" commit_message="BACKPORT: n_tty: Fix unordered accesses to lockless read buffer  Add commit_head buffer index, which the producer-side publishes after input processing in non-canon mode. This ensures the consumer-side observes correctly-ordered writes in non-canonical mode (ie., the buffer data is written before the buffer index is advanced). Fix consumer-side uses of read_cnt() to use commit_head instead.  Add required memory barriers to the tail index to guarantee the consumer-side has completed the loads before the producer-side begins writing new data. Open-code the producer-side receive_room() into the i/o loop.  Remove no-longer-referenced receive_room().  Based on work by Christian Riesch &lt;christian.riesch@omicron.at&gt;  Cc: Christian Riesch &lt;christian.riesch@omicron.at&gt; Signed-off-by: Peter Hurley &lt;peter@hurleysoftware.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman &lt;gregkh@linuxfoundation.org&gt;  [salidoa@google.com: Modied to keep receive_room() which is called     in many places]  BUG=b:29643166 TEST=smaug boots  Change-Id: Ic34d2d578b55e50e8c6004c3241cdafb7789909c (cherry picked from commit 70aca71f92ca2c111978bf676287fab5580d2598) Signed-off-by: Adrian Salido &lt;salidoa@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356730 Commit-Ready: Adrian Salido &lt;salidoa@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Adrian Salido &lt;salidoa@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stephen Barber &lt;smbarber@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="356730" owner_email="salidoa@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/30/356730/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2ad2449c00a59b3eea617d8ca1d797e6c1f18de8" commit="c4b445308b6298f921b10827bf6a5a28a68ac6f2" commit_message="[autotest] Added hack to ignore site logic in cli.  Hack prevents site logic from running on existing deployments where the site file is not deleted but has been merged into the standard file.  BUG=None TEST=locally and on moblab manually  Change-Id: I2ad2449c00a59b3eea617d8ca1d797e6c1f18de8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356692 Commit-Ready: Justin Giorgi &lt;jgiorgi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Justin Giorgi &lt;jgiorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="356692" owner_email="jgiorgi@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/92/356692/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5f4d7612d5cde51a5bcdaa9261594f86ac15a6be" commit="3adcc99718faa1eca55ec2b16e98d6c4604319ba" commit_message="[autotest] Scrub out backslashes in host attributes.  A user can use a ',' in the val portion of the host attribute but they'll need to escape it with two backslashes '\\'.  However when the attribute gets stored, a backslash will be part of the val so if a user did the following:    # atest host mod -i key=val\\,val2\\,val3  The host attribute stored will look like:    key: val\,val2\,val3  This just scrubs out the backslashes in the value.  BUG=None TEST=Check that host can add/mod attributes with '\\,' in the val and doesn't keep the '\\'. Added unit test.  Change-Id: I5f4d7612d5cde51a5bcdaa9261594f86ac15a6be Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356772 Commit-Ready: Justin Giorgi &lt;jgiorgi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="356772" owner_email="kevcheng@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/72/356772/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I424bf0ba952f5ce91ff6e670950a716ff46c45a5" commit="03f291bcb5c4c14f87a8ba431a83c6be3dacfb72" commit_message="cryptohome: Replace scoped_ptr with std::unique_ptr  BUG=none TEST=unit test, install on samus  Change-Id: I424bf0ba952f5ce91ff6e670950a716ff46c45a5 Signed-off-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356165 Reviewed-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="356165" owner_email="gwendal@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/65/356165/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5de28e14aec7d23418bcf4f210143e94489ffd80" commit="33961356dad481512fe519cdfc7f9192cbb044dc" commit_message="moblab: Restrict sudo access  Limit sudo access to a limited number of tools in an effort to secure the moblab platform.  Sudo supported tools: * start * stop * status * restart * mount * dut-control * screen * vi * servod * adb * fastboot * reboot * shutdown  BUG=chromium:394593 TEST=Verified sudo works only with the specified commands.  Change-Id: I5de28e14aec7d23418bcf4f210143e94489ffd80 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/357342 Commit-Ready: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: danny chan &lt;dchan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Michael Tang &lt;ntang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="357342" owner_email="sbasi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/42/357342/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6496574c65889843719da72d3bc461f73c00790a" commit="f07faa2dea81b864f6b0fbff82ede5c3271eeba2" commit_message="Restore GV.NOISE_AMPLITUDES  Previously the list GV.NOISE_AMPLITUDES was accidentally removed.  This is a required constant, so we need to add it back in.  BUG=chromium:620090 TEST=manually tested  Change-Id: I6496574c65889843719da72d3bc461f73c00790a Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/357810 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="357810" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/touch_firmware_test" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/touch_firmware_test" ref="refs/changes/10/357810/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ic6aca34f2ee3245fc71a8632680d1de061afd6ec" commit="346b359574b3e009544bb748688d2c29950627a6" commit_message="CHROMIUM: mali:  disable implicit sync for contexts using explicit sync  Implicit and explicit sync working at the same cause deadlock with multiple contexts sharing buffers. Because Mali does not submit rendering for whole frame atomically, partial jobs from multiple contexts sharing dmabufs interleave and become dependent via implicit sync and deadlock with Android explicit sync fences which are placed at the beginning and end of frame.  This change detects which contexts use explicit Android sync fences and disable implicit sync for them, leaving implicit sync only enabled for synchronizing Chrome context and display driver.  BUG=b:28368490 TEST=run ARC++ on minnie-cheets with early return from CanHandleLayer removed  Signed-off-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/350097 Reviewed-by: David Reveman &lt;reveman@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: Ic6aca34f2ee3245fc71a8632680d1de061afd6ec Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356951 Commit-Ready: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="356951" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/51/356951/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I21415203cb92c2a776383b7453a0512c955280f2" commit="21b54b0ac83204dab0e3264eac6fdf510c6b5a54" commit_message="CHROMIUMOS: hostapd: add and send station connectivity messages over control socket.  Add AUTH,ASSOC,CONNECT and DISCONNECT connectivity event messages and send them over control socket. With each event send additional info like rssi, reason, status and timestamp ..etc.  BUG=None TEST=Connect,disconnect,deauthenticate a station and observe the events       over control socket.  Change-Id: I21415203cb92c2a776383b7453a0512c955280f2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/355012 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Zhihong Yu &lt;zhihongyu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="355012" owner_email="sduvvuri@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="15" project="chromiumos/third_party/hostap" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/hostap" ref="refs/changes/12/355012/15" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I996d0399ce7e8c86c0ef107b2f97974a44b20334" commit="a3fe59025ccc4cac1d659eca0f7e8415cc7b7f00" commit_message="UPSTREAM: Input: uinput - add new UINPUT_DEV_SETUP and UI_ABS_SETUP ioctl  This adds two new ioctls, UINPUT_DEV_SETUP and UI_ABS_SETUP, that replaces the old device setup method (by write()'ing &quot;struct uinput_user_dev&quot; to the node). The old method is not easily extendable and requires huge payloads. Furthermore, overloading write() without properly versioned objects is error-prone.  Therefore, we introduce two new ioctls to replace the old method.  These ioctls support all features of the old method, plus a &quot;resolution&quot; field for absinfo. Furthermore, it's properly forward-compatible to new ABS codes and a growing &quot;struct input_absinfo&quot; structure.  UI_ABS_SETUP also allows user-space to skip unknown axes if not set.  There is no need to copy the whole array temporarily into the kernel, but instead the caller issues several ioctl where we copy each value manually.  Originally-signed-off-by: David Herrmann &lt;dh.herrmann@gmail.com&gt; Originally-signed-off-by: Benjamin Tissoires &lt;benjamin.tissoires@redhat.com&gt; Originally-reviewed-by: David Herrmann &lt;dh.herrmann@gmail.com&gt; Originally-signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dmitry.torokhov@gmail.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 052876f8e5aec887d22c4d06e54aa5531ffcec75)  BUG=chromium:624181 TEST=Manually built kernel and booted a Reks off it. I then was able to successfully run a piece of software using the new features that were added on that Chromebook.  Change-Id: I996d0399ce7e8c86c0ef107b2f97974a44b20334 Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356736 Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="356736" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/36/356736/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iee4c7ade94fcbb82f9b877814df341c2b2c8f7bb" commit="2f31220f1c296f872768bfd8e98b12df9cd2a235" commit_message="Add Stylus support to the touch FW test  This CL adds basic stylus support to the touch FW test by adding an addition state machine for parsing this new protocol.  Styluses use a simpler protocol since there is only a single stylus supported at a time, but essentially it works the same way.  Currently this state machine simply ignores any &quot;hover&quot; events, until we have a better idea of what we want to do with them, but it is capable of parsing that information out as well.  This should allow us to use the same FW test test out stylus-based devices as well as finger-based ones.  To use this new protocol, simply specify --protocol=stylus when running the FW test.  Note: since the autodetection of devices wasn't very useful to start with, and the addition of Stylus made it even more cumbersome and less valuable that's been removed by this patch for simplicity's sake.  BUG=chromium:622067 TEST=manually tested using a device with a styus screen installed  Change-Id: Iee4c7ade94fcbb82f9b877814df341c2b2c8f7bb Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354600 Reviewed-by: Shyh-In Hwang &lt;josephsih@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="354600" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/touch_firmware_test" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/touch_firmware_test" ref="refs/changes/00/354600/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="8524.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>